The paper’s key triage fact is now clear: direct tritangent discovery is an explicit elimination problem (Algorithm 3.1), while the singular-quadric construction gives a much cheaper special route from eight blown-up points (Section 4). That rules out Track A for the proposed family, but it leaves a plausible Track B benchmark if the compact geometric route is materially shorter than exact elimination. I’m checking the authors’ implementation and the repository harness next so those two costs can be measured rather than guessed.
