+"""Verified tritangent-plane generators for arXiv:1805.11702.
+
+The paper studies a smooth degree-six curve C=V(Q,G) in projective 3-space
+and its tritangent planes.  This module stays in those native objects.  It
+inverse-generates a smooth sextic on a quadric cone together with one odd
+tritangent, then carries the curve, a cone parametrisation, and the contact
+divisor through independently sampled projective coordinate changes.
+
+The family is Track B.  Exhausting the finite affine chart of planes costs
+Theta(p^3) exact square tests.  On this distribution there is a compact
+geometric route: the second polar of G in the singular-vertex direction is
+the planted tritangent.  That route is deliberately not used by the
+generator to solve an instance; the certificate is carried from the seed
+identity before the public coordinates are assembled.
+"""
+
