codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator for native finite-field space sextics and tritangent certificates, grounded in Sections 4 and Algorithm 3.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.11702).

Key results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Exact shipping density: 4 valid certificates among 90,438,231,048 candidates.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference enumeration: 462,306 plane tests, 8.08 seconds.
- Compact vertex-polar route: at most 238 operations.
- Answer size: 49 characters, 8 atoms.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/gen_1805_11702.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/README.md)
- [Selftest report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/selftest_report.json)
