The first executable version is in place and the core construction checks at every preset. On the hard preset, the independent tangent-pencil solver actually scans 253,440 cone points and about 254,000 tangent-plane incidences, taking roughly 1.1 seconds and 3.7 million counted finite-field operations; the planted plane verifies by exact polynomial gcd/squarefreeness, not by comparison with the stored answer. I’m running the full gate suite now, including 200,000 structure-aware guesses and coordinate-invariance tests.
