	\noindent
	The genus 1 curve $E \subseteq X$ is defined by the common zero set of $t$ and the defining equation of $X$. Finally, the resulting eight points $\mathcal P'=\{P_1',\ldots,P_8'\}$ are
	\begin{align*}
		P_1'&=(35\!:\!48\!:\!1),& P_2'& = (41\!:\!1\!:\!0),&
		P_3'&=(41\!:\!91\!:\!1),& P_4'& = (61\!:\!1\!:\!0),\\
		P_5'&=(11\!:\!14\!:\!1),& P_6'& = (27\!:\!95\!:\!1),&
