Completed a verified Track B generator based on [arXiv:1805.11702](https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.11702).

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `easy`, \(p=503\)
- Guess resistance: 0/200,000; exact upper bound \(120/503^3=9.4293\times10^{-7}\)
- Five attacks: each 0/8
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, up to 3,714,246 field operations
- Compact second-polar route: 8/8, at most 165 operations
- Bare / structural / placebo oracle arms: each 0/3 solved
- All nine gates and final interface validation pass

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/gen_1805_11702.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1805.11702/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The original eight-point proposal was avoided because Section 4.2 exposes a specialized easy construction. The shipped family instead retains the paper’s native singular-quadric and cubic objects while inverse-generating a certified tritangent through an exact weighted-cubic identity.
